    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nWelcome to No.9 Inishboffin, a beautifully bright and spacious two-bedroom, first-floor apartment boasting breathtaking sea views across to Howth. Nestled behind secure electronic gates and adjacent to the stunning Bulloch Harbour, Bailey View is a well-maintained residential development featuring landscaped communal gardens that border the water's edge. Situated just a stone's throw from the historic and picturesque Bulloch Harbour, and within a short stroll of both Dalkey and Sandycove, Bailey View is convenient to an excellent choice of speciality shops, restaurants, cafés, bars and gastro pubs.\n\nUpon entering, you are immediately welcomed by a sense of space, with well-proportioned living and sleeping areas. The accommodation comprises: Entrance hall, Kitchen/dining room with a charming box bay window, interconnecting doors leading to a spacious living room, which opens onto a private balcony with stunning sea views. Two bedrooms, including a principal bedroom with wall-to-wall fitted wardrobes and a box bay window. The main bathroom completes the accommodation.\n\nThe setting is superb, with scenic walks along Coliemore Road, Harbour Road and Vico Road, as well as the wonderful amenity of Killiney Hill close by. The DART is easily accessible at Dalkey, Sandycove or Glenageary, while the N11 and M50 are both within easy reach, along with bus services on Breffni Road. There is also excellent shopping nearby in Sandycove, Glasthule and Dún Laoghaire."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "\nEntrance Hall - \nWith carpet flooring and a hallway storage press.\n\nBathroom - \nWith tiled floor and tiled walls, full bath, electric shower, wash hand basin with storage, WC, large vanity mirror and central light fitting.\n\nBedroom 1 - \nA large double room with fitted carpet flooring, bay window with side sea view, wall-to-wall fitted wardrobes and wash hand basin.\n\nBedroom 2 - \nA well-proportioned room with carpet flooring, wall-to-wall fitted wardrobes and a large picture window.\n\nKitchen/Dining Room - \nA large kitchen/dining room with a range of wall and floor-level storage cabinets, double-bowl stainless steel sink unit, plumbing for washing machine, space for dryer, oven, four-ring electric hob, fitted shelving and bay window.\n\nLiving Room - \nWith carpet flooring, feature fireplace with open fire, floor-to-ceiling glazing and balcony onto a terrace overlooking the gardens and sea views.\n\n"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "<ul><li>Wrap around external insulation</li><li>Spacious apartment overlooking the sea </li><li>Landscaped communal gardens </li><li>Refurbished platform at the water's edge </li><li>Electronic gates</li><li>Designated car parking</li><li>Guest parking with EV charging</li><li>Annual service charge 3,500 per annum</ul>"
      },
